notes:
Provisional plan ID: infra-m0.6. Native export preserves this ID; acceptance command IDs and test names use the same stable plan identity.
Owner ruling (2026-10-18): a copy on GitHub is enough. The bead's "second verified backup on another medium" is dropped. The copy is the evidence repository DnaCalc/OxFunc-Evidence, holding the files in plain git or in Git LFS; that choice follows the measured feasibility check of 2026-10-18 (file types, sizes, compression, GitHub's limits). The rest of the Do stands:
- hash and deduplicate;
- keep versioned manifests;
- restore a random manifest-selected sample from the GitHub copy and check that it hashes identically to the local originals;
- label legacy data without an Excel fingerprint as unknown.
infra_m0_6__restore_roundtrip reconciles the local inventory with the GitHub copy's inventory, not with two backups. Correction to the Do's wording: OxFunc's git now lists smart-fuzzer/cache (1,618 files, 1.4 GB) and smart-fuzzer/runs (26,774 files, 2.0 GB) as ignored, not as untracked and not ignored (git status --ignored, 2026-10-18). The owner has now named the medium, so this bead can be claimed.
Owner note (2026-10-18): the legacy captures can be recreated from Excel, so this backup is a convenience, not a rescue of irreplaceable data. A fresh capture records the Excel build installed at that time, not the builds that made the legacy files. That fits plan 10.2, under which legacy data without an Excel fingerprint is investigation evidence and never certification. Keep the bead proportionate: copy, manifest and a sample restore check, with no extra machinery.
Feasibility check (2026-10-18, read-only workflow wf_73aa1fd8-7da): the copy already exists. DnaCalc/OxFunc-Evidence (private) has held these files since 2026-10-14 (commit e26b7bdd) in plain git:
- one deterministic gzip blob per file, 28,360 files, 2.70 GB raw stored as 261 MB of gzip, with a GitHub pack of about 220 MiB;
- manifest.tsv (raw and gzip SHA-256 for each file) and archive-evidence.py (archive, verify and restore);
- 32 Intel MKL files (746 MB of third-party, re-downloadable binaries) hashed in excluded.tsv but not stored.
A fresh SHA-256 of all 28,392 current files matched the manifest and excluded.tsv: none changed, none new, none missing. Plain git suits this data and LFS is not needed: per-file gzip shrinks the JSON about elevenfold, the largest blob is 15 MB, under GitHub's 100 MiB block, and LFS on the DnaCalc free org plan would meter clone bandwidth past 10 GiB a month. Storing the raw files would not work, because three are over 100 MiB and the total is over the 2 GB push limit.
Remaining Do under the owner's rulings:
- make verify and restore repository commands, with infra_m0_6__restore_roundtrip reconciling the local inventory with the GitHub copy's manifest;
- implement infra_m0_6__unknown_metadata;
- correct the stale wording (the evidence README's second-backup line, and this bead's 'untracked and not ignored' and 'bulk outside git').
322 run files embed absolute C:/Work/DnaCalc/OxFunc/smart-fuzzer paths, and 238 reference other run or cache folders, so a restore keeps the same relative layout under one root.
Sharpened at claim (2026-10-18):
- Files. The repository commands, `cargo xtask evidence verify [--all | --sample N] [--seed S]` and `cargo xtask evidence restore <dir> [--sample N --seed S]`, live in tools/xtask. They locate the evidence checkout at <legacy root>/OxFunc-Evidence and the originals at <legacy root>/OxFunc/smart-fuzzer; DNACALC_LEGACY_ROOT overrides the root, which is how the WSL clone runs. They run archive-evidence.py with python on Windows or python3 on Linux and report its exit code. The record migration/evidence/oxfunc-smart-fuzzer.json holds:
  - the evidence repository URL and the commit DnaCalc relies on;
  - the manifest's SHA-256 and its counts (archived, excluded, raw and gzip bytes);
  - the layout note: 322 run files embed absolute C:/Work paths, and 238 reference other run or cache folders, so a restore keeps the relative layout under one root;
  - one acquisition label per cache subfolder and run folder: a known Excel build with the place it was read from (a path such as cache/oracle/build-20131, or a metadata field of the capture), or unknown, plus the exact target, if any, the entry can certify.
  The evidence README loses the second-backup line and names the xtask commands. Edit it in C:\Work\DnaCalc\OxFunc-Evidence; the orchestrator commits and pushes it. infra-m0.6 is the only bead that may write there.
- Quarantine reading rule (infra-m0.5): labels for run folders that the numeric-provenance record classes as tainted or unresolved (the W108/W109 identification runs, w108a-reference-hunt among them) come from the path only. Their files are not opened. Elsewhere, read only top-level metadata fields (for example a build, version or Excel field), never the capture content for behaviour.
- Case infra_m0_6__restore_roundtrip:
  - the local evidence checkout is clean, and its HEAD equals both the pinned commit and `git ls-remote origin master`, which is not_run with its reason if the network is down;
  - the local inventory of the two directories equals manifest.tsv plus excluded.tsv by path and size;
  - `cargo xtask evidence restore` of a random sample (at least 100 files, seed printed in an ACCEPT-NOTE) yields files byte-identical to the local originals.
  On a host without the evidence checkout or the originals, the case is not_run with that reason, never passed.
- Case infra_m0_6__unknown_metadata: the record's labels match a recomputation from the paths and permitted metadata. A literal known-build example and a literal unknown example appear in the test. Every unknown entry certifies no Exact target, and a known entry certifies only its own build.
- Platforms: Windows, and Linux in the WSL clone with DNACALC_LEGACY_ROOT=/mnt/c/Work/DnaCalc. No new crate dependencies: the case compares bytes and sizes and needs no hashing crate.
- Class: not adversarial. Proportionate, by the owner's note.
Ruling after round 2 (2026-10-18): the round-2 judge's one blocking finding (no bead owned the 3 builds_outside_rule entries) is resolved by an orchestrator step. dc-h9au now owns that decision, and the record's labels_rule.outside_rule cites it. The orchestrator also corrected three comments that said more than the code does: the restore's access to the originals, the path-only files that the restore sample may byte-compare, and the outside-rule text search. Further follow-ups: dc-h9au (per-row capture builds, local-engine records labelled known, inherited files, counts, registering the evidence commands, the evidence README) and dc-1hwy (evidence folders holding copies of tainted files, to be classified by content). No third implementer round, per the owner's proportionate note.
